{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKrieG5yyhsKnMM6gfBN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Job cleanup now removes Go's read-only module cache, so job homes and worktrees no longer leak. `go test ./internal/...` passes and gofmt is clean. I did not run `make lint`.\n\n- **Cleanup:** `Cleanup` now makes the whole job home and worktree writable before removing them, instead of only the sidecar subtree. It never follows symlinks. The Reaper and the worker's step cleanup both go through `Executor.Cleanup`, so both are covered.\n- **`GOFLAGS`:** host job steps now get `GOFLAGS=-modcacherw`, so a module cache downloaded into a job home is writable from now on.\n- **Shared module cache:** I did not build one, following the plan. A cache that jobs can write to would let one job poison modules that later jobs build. Modules are still downloaded per step, so the slow-tests part of the issue stays open. I'd suggest a separate issue.\n- **Tests:** new `internal/executor/local/cleanup_test.go` covers a 0555 directory holding a 0444 file, an unreadable 0000 directory, a symlink to a read-only tree outside the home (not followed, modes unchanged) and a missing path. I also updated `TestEnvScrubbed` in `local_test.go` to expect the new env var.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` now notes `GOFLAGS`, the per-job module cache and the new cleanup behaviour.\n\nI wrote the report to `.ard/174/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":762,"cache_read_input_tokens":28599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":762},"output_tokens":502,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac2f7b54-4af4-4ec3-b90c-1c15f0b41514","uuid":"a2152eec-